      "rev_n_7_00371b_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_00371b_1",
        "node_id": "n_7_00371b",
        "thought_text": "The previous approach of connecting districts within the same gang and then connecting different gangs may not always produce a valid solution, especially when there are multiple districts in a gang. A more robust approach would be to use a graph coloring technique, where we assign colors (gangs) to districts and ensure no adjacent districts have the same color. This guarantees that all districts are connected while satisfying the condition that directly connected districts belong to different gangs.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-7145663448225800483",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_7_00371b_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_b8c291a232",
        "created_at": 1794528108.4591424
      },
      "rev_n_5_f256d4_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_f256d4_1",
        "node_id": "n_5_f256d4",
        "thought_text": "Instead of using a minimum spanning tree approach, consider using a greedy algorithm to connect districts within the same gang and then connect gangs using a bipartite graph matching technique. This approach ensures all districts are reachable and avoids connecting districts within the same gang.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-6549896922597789389",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_5_f256d4_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_42c679c4e5",
        "created_at": 1794528149.7163575
      },
      "rev_n_8_f48726_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_f48726_1",
        "node_id": "n_8_f48726",
        "thought_text": "The previous approach of using a graph coloring technique or DFS to check reachability is not sufficient. The error occurs because it doesn't guarantee that all districts are connected in a single connected component. A more robust approach would be to use a minimum spanning tree (MST) algorithm, such as Kruskal's algorithm, to connect all districts while ensuring no two directly connected districts belong to the same gang.",
